      "mergeID": "5c9a55b7e604722bc9d639fa",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I play VRChat on desktop mode.\nBut every time I talk, I always hear my own voice!\nEvery time I hear people talk, I don’t see their mouths move as they speak! There’s no mouth movement on every avatar! The ones I’m using have a same problem as well!\nI’m running Windows 7. I need help! A problem I have needs to be fixed!!!",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Hearing myself & no lip sync",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5c522ff4538e7611796a13a7",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I experience the same thing!  I'm on Windows 10 Pro.  I've tried completely reinstalling VRChat to no avail.  I do not hear myself when I use models that have no lipsync (or mouth at all), and I've traced that my voice that echoes back is going through the \"Voices\" channel.  This means I can't just... turn it off to ignore it, because then I won't be able to hear anyone else.  Please fix this soon....",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "5c9a55bfb921f26380013bc4",
      "author": {
        "_id": "59b80cbbd1662e660835c7c5",
