      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "5c9a55bfb921f26380013bc4",
      "mergedPostDetails": "After reinstalling my OS for an unrelated matter, I was having issue after issue involving VRChat.  Most were related to things outside, but one recent one bugs me:  As of two days ago now, all avatars with lip sync now play my voice right back to me, with about a half second delay from me saying it myself.  Moreover, I see no lip sync on any model anymore, including the ones used by others.  This issue apparently lies only in my client, which I've tried reinstalling, repairing, and sifting through.  All I could find is that OVRLipSync.dll can't be found (though it's in the correct spot and holds data; I've checked several times).",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Audio Return, No Lip Sync",
